# AniSource web setup. Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
# Three groups: who you talk to (URLs), secrets that prove it, and optional
# tuning. Anything marked "production: required" fails the deployment closed
# when missing — run `node scripts/verify-anisource-config.mjs --env production`
# before promoting. All of these are server-only: never prefix them with
# VITE_ (the config validator rejects that), and `VITE_ANILIST_API_URL` below
# is the single public exception because Vite bakes it into the client.
#
# An unwanted value is worse than a missing one: every secret must contain at
# least 32 bytes, and every URL must be absolute http(s).

# --- Who you talk to ---
# AniList GraphQL (public metadata). Default lives in config/api-urls.json;
# override here for mocks or a proxy. This is baked into the client bundle.
# VITE_ANILIST_API_URL=https://graphql.anilist.co
# Upstream media API. Default lives in config/api-urls.json. Production must
# be https or the gateway refuses to resolve it.
# ANISOURCE_BASE=
# Second upstream deployment used only when the primary fails. Defaults to the
# fallback URL in config/api-urls.json; set empty to disable.
# ANISOURCE_FALLBACK_BASE=

# --- Secrets (production: required, 32+ bytes each) ---
# Password the gateway shows the API on catalog calls. Must exactly match the
# API's MEDIA_API_SERVICE_TOKEN. Without it nobody can resolve streams.
# ANISOURCE_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# Signs website sessions and ticketed-mode media URLs. Unique random value,
# different from the service token. Without it nobody can watch anything.
# ANISOURCE_SESSION_SECRET=
# Signs direct-mode playback capabilities the API verifies (ADR 0006).
# Comma-separated: the first entry signs, the rest verify during rotation.
# Generate a fresh value, deploy the API with it, then rotate it to first
# place here. Required in production when ANISOURCE_DIRECT_MEDIA is on.
# ANISOURCE_PLAYBACK_SECRETS=

# --- Rate limiting (production: required, set as a pair) ---
# Upstash Redis REST credentials. These are the vendor's names (the Redis
# client expects them); without both, the gateway fails closed in production.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Tuning (safe defaults; touch only with a reason) ---
# Proof-of-work difficulty in leading zero bits (default 20, clamped 1-30).
# Each bit doubles the solver's work: ~1M hashes at 20 is sub-second on
# desktop, seconds on phones, milliseconds for a GPU. Raise under active
# scraping; lower if low-end devices report slow verification. E2E pins 8.
# Networks burning their issuance budget automatically earn +2/+4 bits.
# ANISOURCE_POW_DIFFICULTY=
# Serve API media bytes straight from the API deployment instead of proxying
# them through this gateway (ADR 0004). Catalog JSON still resolves here so
# the service token stays hidden. Accepts 1/true/yes. Enable only after the
# API sets short segment TTLs and the site origin allowlist — and only with
# ANISOURCE_PLAYBACK_SECRETS set, or exposed bearer URLs stay replayable.
# ANISOURCE_DIRECT_MEDIA=
# Playback capability lifetime in seconds (default 900). Shorter shrinks the
# replay window of a copied URL; much shorter forces mid-episode re-resolves.
# ANISOURCE_PLAYBACK_TTL=

# --- Local testing only ---
# Live-smoke override; the smoke test never sends API credentials.
# LIVE_ANISOURCE_BASE=
